{"status": "continue", "message": "Thanks, that's really helpful! Good to know Northwind is a clothing store, so I'll look for the tent elsewhere. The budget ranges are useful too.

To answer your questions: it'll be just me and my sister, so two people. We're heading up to the mountains in Colorado in late January, so it could easily drop to around 0°F at night with some snow. And we'd be driving up to the campsite, not hiking the tent in, so weight isn't a big deal.

Given all that, should I be looking at a 4-season tent in the $400-$700 range? And are there any features you'd especially recommend for snow loading? Also, since I'm going to be buying clothes for this trip anyway, could you tell me what layers Northwind carries for cold-weather camping?"}
